 ### [Screen-Space God Rays](3981-screen-space-god-rays.md)
-Screen-Space God Rays is a real-time post-processing technique that approximates volumetric light scattering (crepuscular rays) by performing per-pixel additive sampling of an image light source in screen space. It simplifies the volume rendering equation to estimate single in-scattering from a single light source, modulated by an estimated occlusion factor derived from radial sampling. Unlike slice-based volume rendering or shadow-map methods, it requires no preprocessing, extra scene geometry, or high fill rate, making it significantly cheaper than volumetric ray marching. However, it is limited to single light sources and lacks full volumetric depth information, leading to artifacts when foreground objects obscure background light shafts.
+Screen-Space God Rays is a real-time post-processing technique that approximates volumetric light scattering (crepuscular rays) by performing per-pixel additive sampling of an image light source in screen space. It builds on [Volumetric Light Shafts (URP Raymarching)](3873-volumetric-light-shafts-urp-raymarching.md) by simplifying the volume rendering equation to estimate single in-scattering from a single light source, modulated by an estimated occlusion factor derived from radial sampling. Unlike slice-based volume rendering or shadow-map methods, it requires no preprocessing, extra scene geometry, or high fill rate, making it significantly cheaper than volumetric ray marching. However, it is limited to single light sources and lacks full volumetric depth information, leading to artifacts when foreground objects obscure background light shafts.
 
 ### [Volumetric Sun Shafts (God Rays)](15833-volumetric-sun-shafts-god-rays.md)
 A post-processing technique that renders volumetric light shafts (sun shafts) by marching a view ray through a sun shadow map, accumulating in-scattered light where the ray is lit and no light where it is shadowed, modulated by ground-hugging haze density. It differs from screen-space alternatives by relying on a dedicated shadow map for occlusion rather than screen-space depth, allowing for more accurate volumetric occlusion from geometry outside the current view frustum, while trading off higher memory bandwidth for the shadow map.
+
+### [Image-Based Light Shaft (Dobashi)](22496-image-based-light-shaft-dobashi.md)
+A method that displays light shafts with a shadow map using texture-mapping hardware by placing parallel slices in front of the screen to compute light scattering induced by atmospheric particles. It uses the color buffer of light received by visible objects to calculate the light frustum from a shadow map and the average extinction of participating media. It sets itself apart from siblings like [Screen-Space God Rays](3981-screen-space-god-rays.md) by explicitly modeling the volumetric light transport equation via parallel slices rather than post-processing screen-space artifacts, and from [Volumetric Sun Shafts (God Rays)](15833-volumetric-sun-shafts-god-rays.md) by relying on hardware-accelerated shadow mapping for occlusion rather than simple radial blurring.
 
